  "core_design": [
    "Flat immutable copiable recipe with typed name, legendary, kind, creature-subtype, keyword and fixed-P/T exceptions; later token exceptions compose after existing overrides.",
    "Effective definition is materialized for shared actual/speculative rule readers. Cold exact-incarnation COW rows retain the physical face, physical token status, original recipe, dormant layers and per-instance restricted-use state. The hot Object gains no fields; CopyKind retains its u8 representation.",
    "Layer-one acquisition identity, static provider chronology and independent hand-size chronology remain distinct. Pure physical retimestamp updates all retained static/hand timestamps without acquiring new intrinsic abilities; hidden layers restore their existing hand chronology.",
    "Copied intrinsic and separately granted programs retain independent origins. A cold opt-in provided-grant row survives the final overlay. Transform timestamp changes preserve uninterrupted grants; actual reattachment/new copy/restore creates a new grant instance. Recipient copying/control changes preserve independent grants.",
    "No copied entry or departure is fabricated. Current providers/targets/layers/legend rules/attachments refresh. Actual departures freeze copied facts before physical normalization. Copy expiry retains generation, counters, damage/tap/combat state and physical identity; ordinary cleanup and turn-ending cleanup perform resulting SBAs.",
    "Owned funding worlds retain recipe and physical identity across virtual departures/entries. Exact entry history covers nonproviders while retaining the existing exact provider-entry order witness. Current type predicates govern basic-land mana, entry counters/tap and nonland/artifact history."
  ],
